E('proportionate','英 /prəˈpɔːʃənət/；美 /prəˈpɔːrʃənət/','相称的；程度适当的；按比例的','大问题用大办法，小问题别用过头的办法，大小或程度配得上。','借自中世纪拉丁 proportionatus，接 proportionare；这里教常用形容词，词尾读 /ət/。',PROPATE,'a proportionate response 是与事情严重程度相称的回应；costs proportionate to income 指费用与收入相称。它常用于判断分量是否合适，不一定是在做严格数学计算。','proportionate to something；a proportionate response；a proportionate share。','proportional 更常用于明确的比例关系；proportionate 常强调适度、相称，但实际用法有重叠。',('The response should be proportionate to the seriousness of the problem.','回应的力度应当与问题的严重程度相称。'),('Each partner received a proportionate share of the proceeds.','每位合伙人都按比例分到了收益。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/proportionate','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/proportionate']),
E('proportionately','英 /prəˈpɔːʃənətli/；美 /prəˈpɔːrʃənətli/','按比例地；相称地','份额或力度随着对应条件一起调整，而不是大家一律拿同样多。','proportionate + -ly；保留形容词末尾的 /ət/，不要漏听成 proportionally。',PROPATE+[['英语 proportionate + -ly → proportionately','相称的 → 按相称关系']],'contribute proportionately 可以是依各自份额出资；respond proportionately 是按事情轻重回应。语气常落在分配是否相称。','contribute proportionately；respond proportionately；proportionately more。','equally 是相等地；proportionately 是按比例地，得到的实际数量可以不同。',('Larger departments contributed proportionately more to the shared fund.','较大的部门按比例向共同基金投入了更多资金。'),('The team adjusted the response proportionately as the risk increased.','随着风险升高，团队相应加大了应对力度。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/proportionately']),
E('proportional','英 /prəˈpɔːʃənl/；美 /prəˈpɔːrʃənl/','成比例的；按比例分配的','一个量改变时，另一个量按相应比例改变，而不是随便一起涨一点。','经法语 proporcionel 或直接借自拉丁 proportionalis；现代可分析为 proportion + -al，但历史形容词不是只在英语里形成。',PROPAL,'directly proportional to 在数学里说正比：一个量加倍，另一个也加倍，比例保持不变。proportional representation 指按票数等比例分配代表席位的制度概念，具体办法可以不同。','directly proportional to；inversely proportional to；proportional representation。','相关 correlated 只说两个量有联系；严格的 proportional 要求相应的比例关系，不是只要一起上升就算。',('At a fixed price per item, the total cost is proportional to the number ordered.','每件单价固定时，总费用与订购数量成正比。'),('The chart uses proportional circles to show the relative sizes of the populations.','图表用大小成比例的圆表示各地人口的相对规模。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/proportional','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/proportional']),
E('proportionally','英 /prəˈpɔːʃənəli/；美 /prəˈpɔːrʃənəli/','按比例地；成比例地','把尺寸或数值一起按同一个比例放大、缩小或分配。','proportional + -ly；拼写 -al + -ly → -ally。',PROPAL+[['英语 proportional + -ly → proportionally','按比例的 → 按比例地']],'resize proportionally 是保持长宽比例缩放；allocate proportionally 是依份额分配。长宽都加同样的绝对数值，未必是在按比例放大。','scale proportionally；increase proportionally；allocate proportionally。','proportionally 和 proportionately 很接近；前者在图形缩放、数量关系里尤其常见。',('The image was reduced proportionally, so its shape did not change.','图片按比例缩小了，因此形状没有改变。'),('The seats were allocated proportionally according to the votes received.','席位按所获票数的比例分配。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/proportionally']),
E('disproportion','英 /ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːʃən/；美 /ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːrʃən/','不相称；比例失衡','把两边摆在一起，发现一边大得太多、重得太多，关系不对称。','dis- 缺乏 + proportion；也可能借自或受法语 disproportion 影响，近源不只一种解释。',DISPROP,'a disproportion between X and Y 指两者不相称。它通常不只是任何差异，而是大小、分量或分配关系显得失衡。','a disproportion between；a striking disproportion；a disproportion in size。','difference 只是不同；disproportion 强调关系不成比例，常隐含不合理或不协调。',('There was a striking disproportion between the effort required and the reward offered.','所需付出与所给报酬之间明显不相称。'),('The drawing’s disproportion makes the tiny doorway look almost comic.','画里失衡的比例让那扇小门看起来近乎滑稽。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/disproportion','https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/disproportion']),
E('disproportionate','英 /ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːʃənət/；美 /ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːrʃənət/','不成比例的；不相称的；过大的','投入、反应或负担与事情本身对不上，常常是一边过头了。','dis- 不 + proportionate；是在相称的形容词前加否定，不是直接从 disproportion 任意补字母。',DISPROPATE,'a disproportionate response 是反应过度或不相称；a disproportionate share 是相对其人数、地位等占了过大的份额。比较基准有时由上下文提供。','disproportionate to；a disproportionate burden；a disproportionate share。','large 只说数量大；disproportionate 说相对某个基准大得不相称。',('A small number of errors caused a disproportionate amount of extra work.','少量错误带来了大得不相称的额外工作量。'),('The penalty seemed disproportionate to the mistake.','处罚看起来与那个错误不相称。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/disproportionate','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/disproportionate']),
E('disproportionately','英 /ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːʃənətli/；美 /ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːrʃənətli/','不成比例地；格外严重地','受到的影响或分到的份额，相比自身人数、规模等显得偏大。','disproportionate + -ly。',DISPROPATE+[['英语 disproportionate + -ly → disproportionately','不相称的 → 以不成比例的方式']],'affect someone disproportionately 说某群体承受的影响相对更大。它不一定表示受影响的绝对人数最多，要看按什么基准比较。','disproportionately affected；disproportionately large；benefit disproportionately。','equally affected 是同等受影响；disproportionately affected 指影响分布失衡。',('The closure disproportionately affected people without cars.','停运对没有汽车的人造成了格外大的影响。'),('A few clients accounted for a disproportionately large share of the complaints.','少数客户的投诉占比大得不相称。'),sources=['https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/disproportionately']),
E('apportion','英 /əˈpɔːʃən/；美 /əˈpɔːrʃən/','分配；分摊；划分责任','先把整体划成份，再决定每人或每组承担哪一份。','借自法语 apportionner、古法语 aporcioner；a- 接拉丁 ad-，后半是法语 portioner 分份，不是英语 a + portion。',APPORT,'apportion costs 是分摊费用；apportion blame 是分派责任、判断谁该负责。这个词不保证一定平均，也不保证分配一定公平。','apportion costs；apportion blame；apportion resources among groups。','divide 只说分开；apportion 常进一步说明把各份分给谁，语体较正式。',('The shared costs were apportioned among the three departments.','共同费用由三个部门分摊。'),('The review focused on solving the problem rather than apportioning blame.','审查的重点是解决问题，而不是分派责任。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/apportion','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/apportion']),
E('apportionment','英 /əˈpɔːʃənmənt/；美 /əˈpɔːrʃənmənt/','分配；分摊；按份分配的结果','把钱怎么分、席位怎么分、责任怎么分这件事作为一个安排来谈。','apportion + -ment，构成行为或结果名词。',APPORT+[['英语 apportion + -ment → apportionment','分配 → 分配过程或安排']],'the apportionment of costs 是费用分摊；政治文字里的 seat apportionment 说席位分配。它可能依人口、份额或其他规则，并不自动等于平均分。','the apportionment of costs；seat apportionment；a fair apportionment。','allocation 也说分配，范围很广；apportionment 更突出整体被分成若干份。',('The contract explains the apportionment of maintenance costs.','合同说明了维护费用的分摊方式。'),('Population changes prompted a review of the apportionment of seats.','人口变化促使有关方面重新审查席位分配。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/apportionment','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/apportionment']),
